          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#chern_insulators Chern insulators
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+state+physics"} solid state physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+insulator"} topological insulator
            which is
            %em not
            “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry+protected+topological+phase"}> protected by any symmetry
            ” has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valence+bundle"} valence bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brillouin+torus"} Brillouin torus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d
            which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundle"} complex vector bundle
            unconstrained by any reality or other conditions, and hence whose class in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+K-theory"} complex K-theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
